Z||000008||rogergarrison||05-10-2001||12:43 PM||||I started dabbling in ebay. You can sell a lot of items where you just front for a wholesaler, they even do all the mailing. Also you can buy stuff and resell it sometimes making a big profit. I bought two Ferrari 328 Diecast cars for $49.00 each and resold one for $217 and the other for $190. I also started rumaging thru house. Im a packrat and alway have to get the lastest gadget. Everything I have stashed in attic and closets is used but like new, I just ebay them. My first week on I just sold some old diecast nascar cars and took in over $500. I even had some stickers made for my cars wheel centers that look like Ferrari. A friend made them and made me 4 sets. I sold all 3 sets i was going to just throw away for $25 each. A member of our car club quit his management job last year to full time sell on another auction site, and he makes over $10,000 a month now working with his wife at home.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-10-2001).]||||reg||1
